# NOTE: `.github/workflows/` used to be ignored here. It never worked as intended — relay-desktop.yml was
# already tracked (ignore rules don't apply to tracked files) while ios.yml sat on disk INVISIBLE to git and
# to GitHub, i.e. a CI workflow that silently did not exist. Workflows reference secrets by NAME only
# (${{ secrets.X }}), never values, so there is nothing here to hide. Tracked deliberately.
# release signing secret — lives ONLY on the release host, never committed.
# (the matching PUBLIC key is baked in: relay-app/release-pubkey.pem + the
#  RELEASE_PUBKEY_PEM constant in scripts/gateway.mjs)
# per-HEAD cached self-update bundle + detached signature (generated on demand)
# catalog publisher secret — pulled from claude/blossom; the matching PUBKEY is
# baked into engine.js / scripts/gateway.mjs as CATALOG_PUB. Loss = forced ecosystem
# rotation (members trust the next-shipped pubkey instead). Anchor on main pre-emptively
# so that if/when Blossom merges, the gitignore is already in place.

# internal-only (not for the public repo)
SECURITY-AUDIT-*.md
*-handoff*.zip
reference/archive/
HANDOFF.md

# local/agent cruft — never publish
.claude/
*.tmp.*
*.bak-*
reference/TrinityOne.zip
reference/nas-relay/
payments-options.html
scripts/.seed-members.json
# a church SECRET key — disposable, but never commit it
scripts/.seed-church.json
scripts/.seed-carekey.json
scripts/.seed-namekey.json
.secrets/

# ── relay runtime data: DEFAULT-DENY. ARCHITECTURE-AUDIT-2026-07-30 ────────────────────────────────────────
# This used to be ~24 individually-named files (relay/relay-db.json, relay/admin.json, relay/vapid.json …).
# That is a denylist, and it failed exactly the way denylists fail here: the store moved from a JSON file to
# SQLite, which created relay.sqlite, relay.sqlite-shm, relay.sqlite-wal and relay-db.json.migrated — four
# names nobody had listed. They were untracked but NOT ignored, so `git add -A` in commit 084b2d4 ("Repo
# tidy (docs-only) … No runtime code touched") swept 640 kB of LIVE RELAY DATABASE into the public repo.
# Untracked two commits later (48186b5) — but git history is permanent, and it is still fetchable
# anonymously today. Contents were a synthetic test church (empty minors/approved lists, encrypted
# journals, joke display names), so the exposure was low; the mechanism was not.
#
# gateway.mjs writes to `TRINITY_DATA_DIR || join(ROOT, 'relay')`, so on any git checkout the LIVE database
# sits inside the working tree by design. The only safe polarity is therefore: ignore the whole directory,
# and re-admit the handful of files that are genuinely source. A new runtime filename is then ignored the
# day it is invented, instead of the day someone remembers to add it.
relay/
!relay/dev-relay.mjs
!relay/deploy/
!relay/deploy/**
relay/rejected.log
scripts/.boot-*.mjs
scripts/.sim-*.json
